WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.041 --> 00:00:01.418
Hello, everyone. 

00:00:01.418 --> 00:00:05.130
20 years ago, Latin American cinema
 exploded around the world.

00:00:05.588 --> 00:00:08.800
From Mexico,
 the names of Alejandro González Iñárritu

00:00:08.967 --> 00:00:13.096
Guillermo del Toro, Alfonso
Cuarón rapidly became a reference

00:00:13.096 --> 00:00:17.142
for everyone around the world
 and not just from Mexico, from Brazil,

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:20.603
there was Walter Salles,
Fernando Meirelles, Padilha.

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:23.648
From Argentina, Trapero,
Lucrecia Martel.

00:00:23.982 --> 00:00:29.446
Many names from Latin America that were
 suddenly setting the bar really high.

00:00:29.654 --> 00:00:32.907
There was no cool festival
if it didn't have a Latin American film.

00:00:34.117 --> 00:00:37.370
Names like "Wild Tales, "Roma," 
"A Fantastic Woman."

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.540
Titles like "Embrace of the Serpent,"
"No," "The Milk of Sorrow."

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:44.002
Latin American films have been 
celebrated around the globe

00:00:44.335 --> 00:00:46.421
and especially at the Academy Awards.

00:00:46.921 --> 00:00:48.590
But we're not stopping there. 

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:51.051
Many filmmakers are crossing over

00:00:51.259 --> 00:00:55.180
and expanding their careers
 into the English language industry,

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:59.851
and those stories need to be heard. 
In the following panel,

00:00:59.976 --> 00:01:05.315
the amazing producer Rosa Bosch will have
a passionate debate with four filmmakers

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:09.110
that are already shooting in English
 that have so much to say

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.987
and experiences to share. 

00:01:10.987 --> 00:01:14.324
So please stay for the panel,
 enjoy the panel

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:17.577
and remember, tell your own stories.

